---

<BlogPost title={title} description={description} publishDate={publishDate} category={category} relatedTools={relatedTools} locale="en">

<div class="lead">
  <p>Need to combine multiple PDF files into one document? Whether you're merging contracts, combining reports, or organizing scattered documents, our free online PDF merger makes it simple.</p>
  <p>No software to download, no sign-up required. Your files stay private on your device.</p>
</div>

<section>
  <h2>Why Merge PDFs?</h2>
  <p>Merging PDFs is essential for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Business reports:</strong> Combine analysis, charts, and appendices into one professional document</li>
    <li><strong>Job applications:</strong> Merge your resume, cover letter, and portfolio into a single PDF</li>
    <li><strong>Legal documents:</strong> Consolidate contracts, addendums, and supporting materials</li>
    <li><strong>Academic work:</strong> Combine research papers, bibliographies, and appendices</li>
    <li><strong>Email attachments:</strong> Send one file instead of multiple attachments</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>How to Merge PDFs: Step-by-Step</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Visit our <a href="/en/tools/merge-pdf/">Merge PDF tool</a></li>
    <li>Upload multiple PDF files (up to 20 files, 100MB total)</li>
    <li>Drag files to reorder them - the top file appears first in your merged document</li>
    <li>Click "Merge PDFs" and download your combined document instantly</li>
  </ol>
  <p>The entire process happens in your browser. Your files never leave your device, ensuring complete privacy for sensitive business documents.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Common Merging Scenarios</h2>

  <h3>Scenario 1: Creating a Complete Report</h3>
  <p>You have a cover page, executive summary, 3 data sections, and appendices as separate files. Arrange them in order and merge into one professional document ready for distribution.</p>

  <h3>Scenario 2: Job Application Package</h3>
  <p>Merge your resume (1 page), cover letter (1 page), and portfolio samples (5 pages) into a single 7-page PDF. Easier for recruiters to review and less likely to get separated.</p>

  <h3>Scenario 3: Monthly Financial Statements</h3>
  <p>Combine invoices, receipts, and summary reports from different departments into one organized monthly statement.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Pro Tips for Better PDF Merging</h2>

  <h3>1. Order Matters</h3>
  <p>Files are merged in the exact order you add them. Double-check the sequence before clicking "Merge" to avoid having to re-merge.</p>

  <h3>2. Compress Large Files First</h3>
  <p>If your individual PDFs are large, use our <a href="/en/tools/compress-pdf/">Compress PDF tool</a> first. This keeps your final merged document under email attachment limits (usually 25MB).</p>

  <h3>3. Remove Unnecessary Pages</h3>
  <p>Before merging, use our <a href="/en/tools/split-pdf/">Split PDF tool</a> to extract only the pages you need. This creates cleaner, more focused merged documents.</p>

  <h3>4. Check Password Protection</h3>
  <p>Password-protected PDFs cannot be merged. Use our <a href="/en/tools/remove-password/">Remove PDF Password tool</a> first to unlock them.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>When to Use Professional Software</h2>
  <p>Our free merger handles most needs perfectly. Consider Adobe Acrobat Pro if you need:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Batch merging (combining hundreds of files automatically)</li>
    <li>Advanced page rearrangement (reorder individual pages across documents)</li>
    <li>Bookmarks and table of contents generation</li>
    <li>Form field merging (combining interactive PDF forms)</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>FAQ</h2>

  <h3>Can I merge different-sized PDFs?</h3>
  <p>Yes! PDFs with different page sizes (A4, Letter, Legal) merge perfectly. Each page retains its original size in the merged document.</p>

  <h3>Is there a limit on file size?</h3>
  <p>You can merge up to 20 files with a combined total of 100MB. For larger batches, split them into groups and merge in stages.</p>

  <h3>Will merging reduce quality?</h3>
  <p>No. Merging is a lossless operation - text, images, and formatting remain exactly as they were in the original files.</p>

  <h3>Can I merge PDFs on my phone?</h3>
  <p>Absolutely! Our tool works on iPhone, Android, tablets, and any device with a modern web browser.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Conclusion</h2>
  <p>Merging PDFs doesn't require expensive software or complicated workflows. With our free online tool, you can combine documents in seconds while keeping your files completely private.</p>
  <p>Try it with your next project - you'll never go back to emailing multiple attachments again!</p>
</section>

</BlogPost>